  "adviceEmergencyUnresponsive": "This is a medical emergency. Call 108 immediately. Do not give anything by mouth. Turn the person on their side and stay with them.",
  "adviceEmergencyBleeding": "Press firmly on the wound with a clean cloth and keep pressing. Call 108 immediately.",
  "adviceEmergencyPoisoning": "Call 108 immediately. Do not try to make the person vomit. Take the container or label with you.",
  "adviceEmergencySnakebite": "Call 108 immediately. Keep the bitten limb still and below heart level. Do not cut, suck or tie the wound. Anti-snake venom is needed urgently.",
  "adviceEmergencyStroke": "Call 108 immediately. Note the time symptoms started, as treatment depends on it. Do not give food or water.",
  "adviceEmergencyChestPain": "Call 108 immediately. Sit and rest, do not walk or drive yourself. This needs an ECG straight away.",
  "adviceEmergencyBreathlessness": "Call 108 immediately. Sit upright and loosen tight clothing. Oxygen may be needed.",
  "adviceEmergencyObstetricBleeding": "Call 108 immediately. Lie down on your left side. Bleeding in pregnancy needs urgent care.",
  "adviceEmergencyLabour": "Go to a facility with delivery services now. Call 108 for transport if needed.",
  "adviceEmergencyFetalMovement": "Go to a facility with obstetric care now. Reduced baby movement needs to be checked urgently.",
  "adviceEmergencySickChild": "Take the child to a facility with paediatric care immediately. Call 108 for transport. Keep the child warm and keep offering fluids if they can swallow.",
  "adviceEmergencyTrauma": "Call 108 immediately. Do not move the injured person unless they are in danger.",
  "adviceEmergencyBurn": "Cool the burn under clean running water for 20 minutes. Do not apply oil, toothpaste or ice. Call 108.",
  "adviceEmergencyAnuria": "Call 108 immediately. Passing almost no urine can mean the kidneys are failing.",

  "adviceHighAnimalBite": "Wash the wound with soap under running water for 15 minutes and go to a facility today. You need rabies vaccination.",
  "adviceHighHaemoptysis": "See a doctor today. You need a chest X-ray and a sputum test to rule out tuberculosis.",
  "adviceHighTbSuspect": "A cough this long with weight loss or night sweats needs a TB test today. Treatment is free.",
  "adviceHighJaundice": "See a doctor today. Yellow eyes or skin needs blood tests to find the cause.",
  "adviceHighBreathlessness": "See a doctor today. Go back or call 108 straight away if breathing gets worse.",
  "adviceHighChestPainYoung": "See a doctor today and ask for an ECG. Call 108 if the pain worsens, spreads to your arm or jaw, or you start sweating.",
  "adviceHighPersistentFever": "Fever this high for this long needs blood tests today to check for dengue, malaria or typhoid.",
  "adviceHighPregnancy": "Any new symptom in pregnancy should be checked the same day at a facility with obstetric care.",
  "adviceHighDiabetesFever": "With diabetes, an infection can worsen quickly. See a doctor today.",
  "adviceHighCardiacHistory": "With your heart history, these symptoms need an ECG today.",

  "adviceMediumDehydration": "Drink ORS after every loose stool. Go to a facility today, and sooner if you cannot keep fluids down or pass very little urine.",
  "adviceMediumAbdominalPain": "See a clinician today. Do not take painkillers on an empty stomach. Go straight away if the pain becomes severe or your abdomen feels hard.",
  "adviceMediumFebrileIllness": "See a clinician today for a check-up and blood tests if needed. Drink plenty of fluids and rest.",
  "adviceMediumUti": "See a clinician today. A urine test is needed. Drink plenty of water in the meantime.",
  "adviceMediumJointPain": "See a clinician for an assessment. Rest the joint and avoid heavy lifting.",
  "adviceMediumMentalHealth": "Talking to a counsellor or doctor helps. You can do this by online consultation, and it is confidential.",
  "adviceMediumVision": "Get your eyes checked. Go sooner if vision loss is sudden or you have eye pain.",
  "adviceMediumMinorBurn": "Cool under running water for 20 minutes, cover loosely with a clean cloth, and get it dressed at a facility.",
  "adviceMediumMinorInjury": "Get the injury cleaned and checked. An X-ray may be needed if there is swelling or you cannot move it.",
  "adviceMediumDental": "See a dentist or the facility doctor. Rinse with warm salt water and avoid very hot or cold food.",

  "adviceLowMildFever": "Rest, drink plenty of fluids and use paracetamol as directed. See a clinician if the fever lasts more than three days, goes above 39C, or you develop breathlessness, a rash or vomiting.",
  "adviceLowMildCough": "Warm fluids and steam inhalation help. See a clinician if the cough lasts more than two weeks, or you get fever, blood in your sputum or breathlessness.",
  "adviceLowMildHeadache": "Rest in a quiet, dark room, drink water and eat regularly. See a clinician if the headache is sudden and severe, or comes with fever, vomiting, weakness or vision changes.",
  "adviceLowSoreThroat": "Warm salt water gargles and warm fluids help. See a clinician if you have difficulty swallowing or breathing, or a fever lasting more than three days.",
  "adviceLowBackPain": "Keep moving gently, avoid bed rest and avoid heavy lifting. See a clinician if the pain spreads down your leg, or you have numbness, weakness or trouble passing urine.",
  "adviceLowRash": "Keep the skin clean and dry and avoid scratching. See a clinician if the rash spreads quickly, blisters, or comes with fever or breathlessness.",
